From 53453a366c29c1cc4877f88d486b3e7e0f8b44bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pento95 <173375476+Pento95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:39:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [hyperinkling] Inkling 2 Mini on Ampere (sm86)

Runs Inkling2Loop on RTX 3090-class GPUs (on top of vllm#69165, which
gates PDL/TMA, e4m3 conversions and the native conv/mix kernels below SM90):
- sm8x takes the SM12x Triton path (use_sm12x_path): Triton relative
  attention and the SM12x low-M bf16 GEMMs (ll_gemm_sm120).
- Routed experts on Marlin MoE (ops/moe_marlin.py): NVFP4, MXFP8 and
  HyperInkling INT4 (AWQ layout, g128 asym, quant format "int4_awq").
- INT8 W8A16 Triton linears (ops/linear_w8.py) for attention, LM head
  (fp32 logits) and token embeddings (optionally in pinned host RAM, UVA),
  behind HYPERINKLING_{ATTN,HEAD,EMBED}_W8 / HYPERINKLING_EMBED_UVA; tiles
  by output width (k/v, o, qkvr, LM head) for decode and verify batches
  (1-128 rows).
- E4M3 KV decode on sm8x as fp16 holding value * 2^-8 (e4m3_f16_scaled):
  the 2^8 goes into the softmax scale and the output, fp16 MMAs.
- sconv conv-state cache backs only each step's tail (SconvStateManager,
  after DFlashSlidingWindowManager): the window, the drafts in flight and
  one hit alignment; the rest of a prefill chunk is null and the conv skips
  stores into the null block; the window below the request's
  shared-prefix junction is backed too (note_shared_prefix).
- Marlin MoE rows in ascending order per expert (order_rows,
  HYPERINKLING_MOE_ORDER, default on): moe_align_block_size leaves them in
  atomic order, and a row's result depends on its Marlin block.
- Decode attention of the full layers: at least two CTAs per SM (21 splits
  at one request instead of 10), +3% decode at 32k, +10% at 128k.
- Loop controllers and sconv dynamic taps on Triton GEMVs (ops/bgemv.py,
  split-K down projection, up to 64 rows) instead of cuBLAS wmma kernels at
  decode and verify sizes.
- Image dummy size follows --limit-mm-per-prompt width/height up to
  4096 px, so pages above 2048 px fit the encoder budget instead of
  waiting forever.
- Calibration capture hook (HYPERINKLING_CAPTURE_DIR) for GPTQ.
- Images over the profiled page (HYPERINKLING_IMAGE_MAX_CELLS, 40 px cells)
  or over the model's 4096 px per side are scaled down (bicubic, aspect
  kept) in the processor instead of waiting forever.
- HYPERINKLING_VISION_HOST=1: the vision tower's weights in pinned host
  RAM, copied to the GPU layer by layer around each layer's forward.
- DSpark drafter: base logits and the Markov fold from the shared INT8 LM
  head (the bf16 head is no longer kept); the fold in INT4/INT8
  (HYPERINKLING_DSPARK_FOLD=w4|w8); draft layers in INT4 g128 RTN on a
  Triton W4A16 kernel (ops/linear_w4.py, HYPERINKLING_DRAFT_W4; split-K below
  16k output columns, one launch above);
  Markov embedding in pinned host RAM with HYPERINKLING_EMBED_UVA; RoPE
  angles computed in-kernel (no cos/sin table growing with max_model_len,
  so --max-model-len -1 costs nothing); draft
  KV as the target's unit-scale E4M3 (HYPERINKLING_DRAFT_KV_FP8, through a
  KV-write-only FlashAttention impl: the draft's attention runs in
  block_decode_attention).
- Online verify length for dynamic speculative decoding
  (v1/spec_decode/dynamic/adaptive_k.py, HYPERINKLING_SPEC_ADAPTIVE): the
  length with the most expected tokens per ms, from decayed per-position
  acceptance and measured decode step times; decode graphs for every
  candidate length.
- Context lookup drafting (HYPERINKLING_LOOKUP=1, ops/lookup.py, after
  HyperQwen's dflash2-lookup-drafting): a suffix match of 8 tokens or more in
  the request's history replaces the DSpark drafts (a choice that never
  depends on them), point masses in the draft-logits cache keep rejection
  sampling exact; the token history is kept on the GPU while it is on.
- sconv metadata: padding rows start at num_actual_tokens, so the
  >256-token tile skip in _sconv_kernel keeps the cache taps of a tile
  that mixes real and padding rows (upstream bug).
- disable_any_whitespace also reaches structural tags, which is how Inkling's
  parser asks for JSON (the server-wide part of vllm#68990).
- Serving, after HyperQwen: --api-key guards every path but /health,
  /ping, /load, /version (auth-deny-default); stall sentinel
  (VLLM_ENGINE_STALL_SENTINEL_S, engine-stall-sentinel); continuous usage
  kept while a tool parser buffers deltas (continuous-stream-usage).
- Turing (sm75), not yet run on one: is_sm75() / is_sm75_or_sm8x() route
  sm75 like sm8x (SM12x Triton path, software e4m3 KV, Marlin experts,
  Triton controller GEMVs); the quant config admits capability 75 and
  fp16 activations; the vision tower runs on per-image SDPA instead of
  FlashAttention 2.
- fp16 activations (use_fp16(): Turing, or HYPERINKLING_FP16=1 on any GPU;
  act_dtype()): buffers, RMSNorm outputs, loop controllers, router weight,
  vision tower and Marlin MoE activations and INT4 scales follow it; the
  W8/W4/bgemv/SwiGLU kernels take their dtype from their pointers (the
  bf16 path is the same code), _situ unpacks fp16 pairs, vision rounding
  uses cvt.rn.f16.f32 (cvt.rn.bf16.f32 is SM80+); bf16 checkpoint tensors
  are cast at load, clamped at fp16's range and logged; the sconv SWA cache
  takes fp16. Requires --dtype float16.
- DSpark in fp16: the draft's bf16 (and fp32) checkpoint tensors are cast at
  load with the same saturation, the Markov fold clamped to fp16's range;
  the draft kernels (Q/K norm + RoPE, softcap, Markov gate) store in their
  pointers' dtype (the gate keeps its bf16 roundings, as bit operations);
  the draft KV accepts float16. On sm75 the draft's RMSNorms run on a
  Triton kernel (add_rms_norm_) instead of flashinfer's, which JIT-compiles
  with the host's nvcc there.
- Load-time conversions in chunks (quantize_int8 by 4096 rows, the fp16
  saturating cast by 16M values; results unchanged): the fp32 temporaries
  of the 201k-row LM head and embeddings no longer overflow a 22 GB card.
- Turing's 64 KB of shared memory per block: relative attention takes
  BLOCK_M <= 64 and BLOCK_N 64 (BLOCK_M <= 32) or 32 on sm75 (the sm86
  tiles took 72-96 KB there).
- W8 linears on sm75: Triton emits no tensor-core MMA there and tl.dot ran
  as FMA through shared memory (80% of a 2080 Ti decode step, ~2 ms a
  call). Up to 64 rows: _w8_gemv_kernel (3D tiles of rows x outputs x K,
  products accumulated elementwise, one K reduction at the end; tiles
  measured on a 2080 Ti in sm75_gemv_tile); above: dequantized 8192-row
  blocks on cuBLAS. The same kernel without scales (gemv_sm75) serves
  k_group_partials up to 64 rows on sm75 (MoE router, sconv taps, already
  summed), and linear_k_groups above that runs on cuBLAS; the K-group
  summation order is not kept there. Its axis 2 batches and splits K
  (bgemv_sm75): the decode-size loop controllers run on it on sm75
  (controller_gemv_sm75, the rank-R down projection in 8 K slices, which
  the up projection sums in fp32, in order, as it loads them).
- Attention on sm75 (ops/attention_sm75.py): prefill (MODE_OUT_LSE, full
  and sliding-window layers) and the full layers' split decode partials
  (MODE_PARTIAL, at most 64 rows; any GQA group up to 16, the model has
  3 heads per KV head; blocks per SM by the block's warps, measured;
  HYPERINKLING_SM75_PREFILL_WARPS=8 for 128-row prefill blocks on the
  full layers; the local layers' short launches stay on
  Triton, and the first launch of each kind logs which kernel serves and
  why) over the E4M3 byte cache, from a CUDA wmma kernel
  of the HyperInkling repository (kernels/sm75, loaded through ctypes
  from HYPERINKLING_SM75_LIB, launched on torch's stream), as the Triton
  kernel's dots run on FMA there (74% of an 8k prefill and ~43 ms of a
  decode step at 90k tokens on a 2080 Ti). With the library,
  plan_decode_attention gives full layers HYPERINKLING_SM75_ATTN_CTAS (4)
  one-warp blocks per SM; without it the Triton kernel serves.
- k_group_partials above 64 rows on sm75: cuBLAS (the prefill router took
  97 ms per 1000 tokens on the FMA-bound Triton kernel).
- HYPERINKLING_FP16_CHECK=1: Inkling2LoopModel.forward logs each new record
  of the residual stream's max |value| above 4096, and any non-finite
  value, by layer and pass (fp16 headroom on Turing; run eager).

